Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall not commence later than the expiration of 3 years beginning with the date of this planning permission.

Condition required to be imposed by section 91(1)(a) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended by section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004).
Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in complete accordance with the following approved drawings, other than where those details are altered pursuant to the conditions of this planning permission:

P/01 rev A;
P/02 rev A; 
P/03; 
P/04; 
P/05; 
P/06; 
P/07 rev A; 
P/08; 
P/09; 
P/11 rev A; 
P/12; 
P/13.

To ensure full compliance with the planning application hereby approved and to prevent harm arising through deviations from the approved plans.
Condition : 3 - The development hereby approved shall be carried out and completed in accordance with the materials (including colour and finish) specified on the drawings hereby approved. The development shall be permanently retained in accordance with the approved details. Any works of making good to existing elevations shall be carried out in materials to match the elevation to which the works relate.  

To ensure a satisfactory external appearance, in accordance with Policies DC1 and DC4 of the Local Plan (2018).
Condition : 4 - The terraces hereby approved shall not be first used until the privacy screening has been installed as shown on approved drawing nos. P/03, P/04, P/07 rev A, P/08 and P/11. The privacy screen shall achieve a minimum level of obscurity equivalent to Pilkington Texture Glass Level 3 and shall have a height of 1.7m above the finished floor level of the terrace along the side and rear elevations. The privacy screen shall thereafter be permanently retained as approved.  

To protect the amenities of neighbouring occupiers in terms of overlooking and privacy in accordance with Policy HO11 of the Local Plan (2018).
Condition : 5 - The remainder of the roof of the existing back addition, other than the area shown as a terrace on the approved plans, shall not be converted into or used as a terrace or other open amenity space. No alterations shall be carried out; nor planters or other chattels placed on the remainder of the roof of the back addition or the extension hereby approved. No railings or other means of enclosure shall be erected around the roof and no alterations shall be carried out to the property, including the extension hereby approved, to form an access onto the roof.   

Such a use would be detrimental to the amenities of neighbouring properties by reason of overlooking and loss of privacy and potential noise and disturbance, contrary to Policies CC11 and HO11 of the Local Plan (2018).
Condition : 6 - The first floor glazed extension hereby approved shall not be first used until the obscure-glazing to the side elevations has been installed as shown on approved drawing nos. P/03, P/07 rev A, P/08 and P/09. The obscure glazing shall achieve a minimum level of obscurity equivalent to Pilkington Texture Glass Level 3. The obscure glazing shall thereafter be permanently retained as approved.  

To protect the amenities of neighbouring occupiers in terms of overlooking and privacy in accordance with Policy HO11 of the Local Plan (2018).
